  "_why_this_file_exists": [
    "There is no such thing as a list of every channel. No platform sells one",
    "and none of them expose an enumeration endpoint: YouTube and Twitch answer",
    "questions about an id you already have, TikTok and Instagram answer only",
    "about the account that connected. The only way to get a complete list is to",
    "scrape, which this project does not do.",
    "",
    "So the database is seeded and then enriched. This file is the seed: the",
    "channels worth having, chosen by a person. build.js resolves each one",
    "through the official API, measures it, runs it past the safety rules and",
    "writes the result. Adding a channel means adding a line here.",
    "",
    "Entries are handles, not ids. A handle is what you can read off a channel",
    "page and verify; a UC id copied from memory is a channel nobody can check.",
    "The API resolves handle -> id at build time, and anything that fails to",
    "resolve is written to unresolved.json instead of being quietly dropped."
  ],

